# Rust build output
/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# Local player profile: identity keys, settings, hand history.
#
# The client is portable, so the profile lives next to the binary - which
# means it can appear at any depth, wherever somebody ran one. Unanchored
# for exactly that reason: `/profile/` matched the root only, and a client
# run from a tracked subdirectory would have written an unignored key pair.
profile/
/dist/

# Editor / OS noise
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
/vendor/**/target/
/profile/

# The vendored C for D-019's Tox transport, fetched at pinned commits by
# tools/build-tox.ps1 rather than committed. 12.7 MB for a transport whose
# whole point - a measurement across two networks - has not been taken yet;
# the script carries the argument and the hashes, and says what would change
# the answer. `vendor/ziffle` IS committed, so this is the exception and not
# the rule.
/vendor/c-toxcore/
/vendor/libsodium/
